WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Electricity runs everything in an HVAC system. If you don't understand it, you
can't diagnose anything.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:01:12.000
This quiz tests Ohm's Law calculations, meter usage, wiring diagram reading,
capacitor diagnosis, contactor operation, and electrical safety. You must be
able to calculate voltage, current, or resistance given the other two values,

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:48.000
Here's why this matters on the job: Electrical knowledge separates a
parts-changer from a real technician. Anyone can swap a capacitor — a technician
understands WHY it failed and checks for the root cause.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:02:24.000
Watch out for these: Know Ohm's Law cold: V=IR, I=V/R, R=V/I. And — Know the
difference between series and parallel circuits

00:02:24.000 --> 00:03:00.000
Take a minute before you move on. What's the one thing from this lesson you need
to remember on a service call?

